# ============================================================================
# Keystone — environment configuration
# ============================================================================
# Copy this to .env.local. You fill in:
#   1. SUPRSEND_SERVICE_TOKEN below, then
#   2. each workspace's Workspace Key + Secret from the dashboard (README step 4).
# Running `node --env-file=.env.local scripts/provision.mjs workspaces` creates the
# workspaces and auto-fills their public key + signing key.
#
# .env.local is gitignored — your secrets never get committed.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# REQUIRED — your SuprSend ACCOUNT service token.
# (Dashboard → Account Settings → Service Tokens → generate → paste here)
SUPRSEND_SERVICE_TOKEN=

# The `workspaces` command APPENDS these per-workspace lines below (per customer):
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPRSEND_<WS>_PUBLIC_KEY       (in-app inbox)     — auto-filled
#   SUPRSEND_<WS>_SIGNING_KEY_ID / _B64        (template editor)  — auto-filled
#   SUPRSEND_<WS>_WORKSPACE_KEY / _SECRET      (backend login)    — YOU paste (dashboard)

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional — leave unset unless you need them:
#   SAFE_TEST_EMAIL_USER / SAFE_TEST_EMAIL_DOMAIN  where demo emails route
#                                                  (default: nikita+<name>@suprsend.com)
#   OPENAI_API_KEY                                 only for the AI "Generate" button
#                                                  on Message Templates
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
